      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While boycotting feels like a principled stand, it is a passive surrender that gives the very forces you oppose the perfect victory. Protest through absence is merely handing control to the loudest, most entrenched voice in the room. A true protest requires aggressive engagement: show up, vote against the worst, and then organize to dismantle the system from within. To refuse to participate is to concede the ground to those who willfully ignore your concerns.",
      "source": "target",
